incident_description:
1.) I PURCHASED SALOMON SPEEDCROSS 3 M+S TRAIL RUNNING SHOES A COUPLE YEARS BACK, BUT HAVE RUN ON THEM VERY LITTLE SINCE;
2.) THE LACE OF THE RIGHT SHOE BROKE. SALOMON USES A PROPRIETARY LACE SYSTEM FOR THESE SHOES;
3.) I ORDERED THE REPLACEMENT LACES - A ?QUICKLACE? SYSTEM - FROM SALOMON;
4.) AFTER A LENGTHY INSTALLATION PROCESS, I FINALLY INSTALLED THE NEW LACES TO FACTORY SPECIFICATIONS. ONCE I FINALLY HAD THE LACES PROPERLY INSTALLED, I WAS SHOCKED TO FIND THAT IT CREATED A SAFETY HAZARD, NAMELY: THAT THE BLACK PLASTIC PART THAT CONNECTS THE TWO ENDS OF THE LACES IS SO HEAVY IN THE REPLACEMENT KIT THAT IT WORKS ITS WAY OUT OF THE SALOMON-PROVIDED MESH POCKET VERY QUICKLY WHEN IN USE, CAUSING A TRIPPING HAZARD. THE REPLACEMENT COMPONENT IS HEAVIER AND LARGER THAN THE ORIGINAL, WHICH IS WHAT CAUSES THIS PROBLEM;
5.) I CONTACTED SALOMON, EXPLAINED THE PROBLEM AND SAFETY RISK TO THEM. NOT ONLY DID THEY NOT EXPRESS CONCERN FOR THE SAFETY HAZARD I REFERENCE, THEY ALSO WERE UNWILLING TO WORK WITH ME TO RESOLVE MY SPECIFIC CONCERNS.

I WOULD LIKE THE FOLLOWING RESOLUTIONS:
1.) FOR SALOMON'S "QUICKLACE" PRODUCT, AS IT IS NOW, TO BE REMOVED THE MARKET AND RECALLED;
2.) FOR SALOMON TO DEVELOP A NEW, SAFER LACE SYSTEM;
3.) FOR SALOMON TO ISSUE ME A FORMAL APOLOGY, AND PROVIDE ME WITH A REPLACEMENT SET OF SHOES.

THANK YOU FOR YOUR ASSISTANCE,

[REDACTED]
